# rsdl-diag-showcase coverage notes

This package is crafted so its compile emits one instance of every diagnostic
the rsdl profile implements. The `@rsdl-diag-showcase` diagnostics snapshot
(`crates/ridlc/tests/snapshots/`) is the rsdl diagnostic index, the way
`ridl-diag-showcase` is for the ridl codes. `RSDL_PROFILE_CODES` in
`crates/ridlc/tests/corpus.rs` is the machine-checked index.

One file per diagnostic family, so a parse error in one family never suppresses
a check in another:

- `profile_boundary.rsdl` — the parser's rsdl codes: RSDL-604 for a declaration
  of another profile, and FORM-102 for `internal` before an rsdl keyword.

A code the showcase cannot provoke in one compile is listed in
`RSDL_PROFILE_CODES` as `Elsewhere`, with the fixture that provokes it.
